==Campaign==

===Erdoğan campaign===
{{Main|Recep Tayyip Erdoğan presidential campaign, 2018}}
Recep Tayyip Erdoğan, incumbent [[President of Turkey]] since 2014, was officially nominated as the presidential candidate of the Justice and Development Party (AKP) on 3 May 2018.<ref>{{cite web|title=AKP formally nominates Erdoğan for presidential election|url=http://www.hurriyetdailynews.com/akp-formally-nominates-erdogan-for-presidential-election-131254|website=Hürriyet Daily News|access-date=4 May 2018}}</ref> Shortly thereafter, the nominally oppositional Nationalist Movement Party (MHP) reiterated that it would endorse Erdoğan's candidacy, and would jointly apply to the electoral commission for its formal registration.<ref>{{cite web|title=AKP, MHP jointly apply to election board for Erdoğan's presidential bid|url=http://www.hurriyetdailynews.com/akp-mhp-jointly-apply-to-election-board-for-erdogans-presidential-bid-131311|website=Hürriyet Daily News|access-date=4 May 2018}}</ref> In early May, it was confirmed by Erdoğan that he would be visiting the [[Bosnia]]n capital of [[Sarajevo]] in the early stages of the campaign, most likely on 20 May 2018, and hold campaign rallies with the [[Turks in Bosnia and Herzegovina|Bosnian Turks]] to drum up support for his re-election bid.<ref>{{cite web|title=Erdogan's Bosnia Rally May Be Key Game-Changer|url=http://www.balkaninsight.com/en/article/erdogan-s-bosnia-rally-may-be-key-game-changer-05-04-2018|website=Balkan Insight|date=4 May 2018|access-date=4 May 2018}}</ref>

===İnce campaign===
[[File:CHP 2018 manifesto launch 1.jpg|thumb|[[Muharrem İnce]] at the [[Republican People's Party|CHP]] manifesto launch, 26 May]]
{{Main|Muharrem İnce presidential campaign, 2018}}
Muharrem İnce, a [[member of parliament]] for [[Yalova]], was announced as the presidential candidate of the Republican People's Party (CHP) on 3 May 2018.<ref name="auto"/> On the following day, 4 May, party leader [[Kemal Kilicdaroglu]] formally proclaimed the CHP's support for İnce.<ref name="auto1"/> Shortly thereafter, the CHP began preparations for the campaign season, launching the production of campaign material and merchandise. It was revealed in early May that İnce's campaign would adopt the slogan "''Türkiye'ye güvence Muharrem İnce''", roughly translating to "Muharrem İnce, an assurance to Turkey",<ref>{{cite web|title=İşte Muharrem İnce'nin afişi ve sloganı|url=http://www.cumhuriyet.com.tr/haber/siyaset/968571/iste_Muharrem_ince_nin_afisi_ve_slogani.html|website=Cumhuriyet|access-date=4 May 2018}}</ref> and that it would be kicked off with an election rally in his home city of [[Yalova]] on 5 May.<ref>{{cite web|title=CHP presidential candidate İnce vows to be 'everyone's president'|url=http://www.hurriyetdailynews.com/chp-presidential-candidate-ince-vows-to-be-everyones-president-131298|website=Hürriyet Daily News|access-date=4 May 2018}}</ref>

===Demirtaş campaign===
[[File:Selahattin Demirtaş 2018 campaign launch.jpg|thumb|Selahattin Demirtaş's campaign being launched outside [[Edirne]] prison where he is incarcerated, 25 May]]
{{Main|Selahattin Demirtaş presidential campaign, 2018}}
Selahattin Demirtaş was officially announced as the candidate of the People's Democratic Party (HDP) on 4 May 2018, after members of the party had hinted at his candidacy weeks in advance.{{citation needed|date=November 2020}} Party leader [[Pervin Buldan]] declared that Demirtaş, a jailed former co-chair of the HDP, would be leading a five-party "Kurdish alliance" into the general election.<ref>{{cite web|title=HDP nominates imprisoned former leader Demirtaş for presidency|url=http://www.hurriyetdailynews.com/hdp-nominates-imprisoned-former-leader-demirtas-for-presidency-131350|website=Hürriyet Daily News|access-date=4 May 2018}}</ref>

===Akşener campaign===
{{Main|Meral Akşener presidential campaign, 2018}}
Meral Akşener was nominated as the candidate of the İyi Party on 4 May 2018, after she had successfully collected the 100,000 signatures required for minor party candidates to gain ballot access. Reportedly, she passed this threshold less than four hours after having launched her signature collection campaign.<ref>{{cite web|title=Akşener collects 100,000 signatures in 4 hours to become presidential candidate|url=https://www.turkishminute.com/2018/05/04/aksener-collects-100000-signatures-in-4-hours-to-become-presidential-candidate/|website=Turkish Minute|access-date=4 May 2018}}</ref>

===Karamollaoğlu campaign===
[[File:Temel_Karamollaoğlu_presidential_campaign.jpg|thumb|Temel Karamollaoğlu beginning his campaign on 1 May]]
{{Main|Temel Karamollaoğlu presidential campaign, 2018}}
Temel Karamollaoğlu was nominated as the candidate of the Felicity Party (SP) on 6 May 2018, after he had successfully collected the 100,000 signatures required for minor party candidates to gain ballot access. Karamollaoğlu's campaign adopted the slogan "''Türkiye'ye bilge başkan''" ("A wise leader for Turkey").

=== Perinçek campaign ===
{{Main|Doğu Perinçek presidential campaign, 2018}}
Doğu Perinçek was nominated as the candidate of the [[Patriotic Party (Turkey)|VATAN]] Party on 9 May 2018, after he had successfully collected the 100,000 signatures required for minor party candidates to gain ballot access.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.aydinlik.com.tr/baraj-yikildi-dogu-perincek-100-bini-asti-politika-mayis-2018-11|title=Baraj yıkıldı: Doğu Perinçek 100 bini aştı! - Aydınlık|first=Aydınlık|last=Gazetesi|date=8 January 2016}}</ref>

